cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Image Color Analysis Tool"
abstract: "A Python tool for analyzing colors in images, providing detailed information about color distributions, harmonies, and color space conversions (RGB, HEX, CMYK, OKLab, OKLCh). Features include deterministic perceptual palette extraction (k-means++ clustering in OKLab), OKLCh color harmony calculations (complementary, analogous, triadic, tetradic), ICC-based CMYK conversion (FOGRA39), WCAG 2.2 and APCA contrast reporting, single image and batch processing, dominant color detection, flexible output formats (plain text, JSON, and CSS/Design Tokens), design token export compatible with the W3C Design Token Community Group format and Tailwind CSS v4, and support for multiple image formats (PNG, JPG, TIFF, WebP, PSD)."
